1
00:00:10,793 --> 00:00:12,229
Hey.

2
00:00:12,316 --> 00:00:14,840
Hey, boss. I got your text.
What's up?

3
00:00:14,927 --> 00:00:17,104
I got a call
from the FBI.

4
00:00:17,191 --> 00:00:18,757
What do they want?

5
00:00:18,844 --> 00:00:22,457
It's about the investigation
of Craig O'Laughlin's death.

6
00:00:22,544 --> 00:00:23,632
Oh.

7
00:00:23,719 --> 00:00:25,547
It was an agent
named Wexler.

8
00:00:25,634 --> 00:00:27,592
He said he'd been
trying to reach you.

9
00:00:27,679 --> 00:00:29,246
Yeah, he left some messages.

10
00:00:29,333 --> 00:00:31,901
I haven't called him back.
What did he say?

11
00:00:31,988 --> 00:00:34,947
The investigation's over.
They've filed the report.

12
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:38,081
He just wanted you to know that
he was returning your necklace.

13
00:00:38,168 --> 00:00:39,169
My what?

14
00:00:39,256 --> 00:00:41,128
The necklace
O'Laughlin gave you.

15
00:00:41,215 --> 00:00:43,434
It was in evidence,
but they're done with it.

16
00:00:43,521 --> 00:00:44,870
He sent it over.

17
00:00:44,957 --> 00:00:47,090
I don't..

18
00:00:47,177 --> 00:00:49,223
Look, I don't want it.
You take it.

19
00:00:49,310 --> 00:00:51,529
If you don't want it,
you can sell it

20
00:00:51,616 --> 00:00:53,357
or take it
to the evidence room

21
00:00:53,444 --> 00:00:55,316
and they can auction it off.

22
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:00,799
Here, it's for you.

23
00:01:00,886 --> 00:01:02,801
[gunshots]

24
00:01:05,543 --> 00:01:07,328
Hey, boss..

25
00:01:07,415 --> 00:01:10,505
Caught one. Shooting victim
out in El Oro State Forest.

26
00:01:10,592 --> 00:01:12,507
You two take it.

27
00:01:12,594 --> 00:01:15,031
- Grace? Are you okay?
- Fine, yeah.

28
00:01:15,118 --> 00:01:17,686
- You want me to take it away?
- No, it's okay.

29
00:01:17,773 --> 00:01:20,950
El Oro State Forest, that's
East of Lake Tahoe, right?

30
00:01:21,037 --> 00:01:22,430
Yeah.

31
00:01:30,655 --> 00:01:33,528
[instrumental music]

32
00:01:44,930 --> 00:01:46,236
You get lost?

33
00:01:46,323 --> 00:01:48,020
Briefly.

34
00:01:48,108 --> 00:01:51,459
Beautiful out here, though they
could use a little more signage.

35
00:01:51,546 --> 00:01:53,156
Victim's name's
Gabriel Porchetto Junior.

36
00:01:53,243 --> 00:01:54,853
Father's a big mob boss.

37
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:57,900
Runs narcotics and illegal
gambling in the Northeast.

38
00:01:57,987 --> 00:02:00,468
They live in the city.
This is a vacation house.

39
00:02:00,555 --> 00:02:03,775
"Porchetto"
that's Argentinian, I believe.

40
00:02:03,862 --> 00:02:04,994
How can you tell?

41
00:02:05,081 --> 00:02:07,301
I used to read
a lot of phone books.

42
00:02:07,388 --> 00:02:10,042
As I recall, Buenos Aires
had many Porchettos.

43
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:11,914
You used to read phone books.

44
00:02:12,001 --> 00:02:15,961
Yes, it's an excellent mnemonic
exercise. You should try it.

45
00:02:16,048 --> 00:02:18,486
[Cho]
'Porchetto and his younger
brother were throwing a party.'

46
00:02:18,573 --> 00:02:19,965
'Had a half-dozen friends here.'

47
00:02:20,052 --> 00:02:21,619
Brought in hookers
for entertainment.

48
00:02:21,706 --> 00:02:23,578
Good, wholesome fun.

49
00:02:23,665 --> 00:02:25,971
There's a security fence
around the entire compound.

50
00:02:26,058 --> 00:02:27,712
About a hundred yards
that way

51
00:02:27,799 --> 00:02:29,801
there's a blanket
thrown over the barbed wire

52
00:02:29,888 --> 00:02:32,500
and footprints inside and out.
Looks like the point of entry.

53
00:02:32,587 --> 00:02:33,979
Hmm.

54
00:02:34,066 --> 00:02:35,981
And here we are.

55
00:02:42,031 --> 00:02:43,163
Ugh.

56
00:02:44,642 --> 00:02:46,470
Which one's
the younger brother?

57
00:02:47,906 --> 00:02:49,212
Sergio.

58
00:02:52,607 --> 00:02:53,999
Yeah?

59
00:02:54,086 --> 00:02:56,959
So you're Sergio,
and, uh...who are you?

60
00:02:57,046 --> 00:02:59,135
Curtis Nett.
I work for the family.

61
00:02:59,222 --> 00:03:00,397
The enforcer.

62
00:03:00,484 --> 00:03:02,486
I work for the family.
Ten years.

63
00:03:02,573 --> 00:03:03,922
Just tell us what happened.

64
00:03:04,009 --> 00:03:06,577
We were inside
the house, partying.

65
00:03:06,664 --> 00:03:09,624
Gabe came out to the hot tub
with one of the girls.

66
00:03:09,711 --> 00:03:12,192
There's a shot.
Curtis and I run out and..

67
00:03:13,628 --> 00:03:16,500
Gabe's...you know.

68
00:03:16,587 --> 00:03:18,241
Girl's freaking out.

69
00:03:18,328 --> 00:03:21,331
I run to the fence.
I see a guy just climbed over.

70
00:03:21,418 --> 00:03:24,421
I throw a shot at him.
He throws a shot at me.

71
00:03:24,508 --> 00:03:26,467
No one hit anything.
He takes off running.

72
00:03:26,554 --> 00:03:28,033
You get a look at him?

73
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:30,122
White guy, jacket,
baseball cap.

74
00:03:30,210 --> 00:03:32,124
'You gave your gun
to the sheriff, right?'

75
00:03:32,212 --> 00:03:33,735
That's right.

76
00:03:33,822 --> 00:03:36,303
We need all the other guns
even the ones hidden.

77
00:03:36,390 --> 00:03:39,393
Look at this mess. You want to
talk some crap weapons charges?

78
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:40,872
We won't necessarily
press charges

79
00:03:40,959 --> 00:03:43,135
but I need every gun
for a ballistics check.

80
00:03:43,223 --> 00:03:44,746
I'll tell the guys.

81
00:03:44,833 --> 00:03:47,139
You do that, Serge.

82
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:48,750
So what's the deal?

83
00:03:48,837 --> 00:03:51,840
You work for the family,
but you have no respect for him.

84
00:03:51,927 --> 00:03:53,015
Is that a question?

85
00:03:53,102 --> 00:03:54,625
I don't know. Was it?

86
00:03:54,712 --> 00:03:57,280
Where's the girl?
That's a question.

87
00:04:00,501 --> 00:04:02,503
[sighs]
Her name is Janpen.

88
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:04,722
She's Chinese.
Doesn't speak English.

89
00:04:04,809 --> 00:04:07,899
Okay. Hi.

90
00:04:07,986 --> 00:04:09,423
My name is Patrick.

91
00:04:09,510 --> 00:04:12,077
[speaks Chinese]

92
00:04:13,383 --> 00:04:16,256
We're gonna need
a translator.

93
00:04:16,343 --> 00:04:19,215
What is that hideous thing
on her shoulder?

94
00:04:19,302 --> 00:04:21,261
[singsongy]
She speaks English.

95
00:04:21,348 --> 00:04:23,350
She's just a little
bit shy, right?

96
00:04:25,352 --> 00:04:27,745
I don't speak English.
Guys don't talk to me.

97
00:04:27,832 --> 00:04:29,356
It's better that way.

98
00:04:29,443 --> 00:04:31,880
So what did you see
when Mr. Porchetto was shot?

99
00:04:31,967 --> 00:04:35,100
Nothing. There's a loud bang
scares the crap out of me, and..

100
00:04:35,187 --> 00:04:37,755
...the guy's dead. I mean,
I freaked out. That's it.

101
00:04:37,842 --> 00:04:39,017
What'd the shooter
look like?

102
00:04:39,104 --> 00:04:40,410
Didn't see him.

103
00:04:40,497 --> 00:04:42,456
You're a good liar.
Good, not great.

104
00:04:42,543 --> 00:04:44,284
She saw him close up.

105
00:04:44,371 --> 00:04:46,851
I know who these guys are,
I'm not getting involved.

106
00:04:46,938 --> 00:04:48,288
Maybe you shot him.

107
00:04:48,375 --> 00:04:50,551
Yeah, I hid the gun
in my pants.

108
00:04:50,638 --> 00:04:52,901
I'm taking you in.
We'll talk at the office.

109
00:04:52,988 --> 00:04:54,685
I don't have to go with you.

110
00:04:54,772 --> 00:04:56,383
I could arrest you
for prostitution..

111
00:04:56,470 --> 00:04:58,559
...is that how
you want to do it?

112
00:04:58,646 --> 00:05:00,691
Well, can I put
some clothes on first?

113
00:05:00,778 --> 00:05:02,171
Sure.

114
00:05:08,046 --> 00:05:10,571
Interesting girl.

115
00:05:12,137 --> 00:05:13,574
So what's
your take on this?

116
00:05:13,661 --> 00:05:16,185
Well, the fresh air,
my first mob hit..

117
00:05:16,272 --> 00:05:17,752
I'm thrilled.

118
00:05:54,005 --> 00:05:55,442
[shuts glove compartment]

119
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:00,621
What?

120
00:06:00,708 --> 00:06:03,450
The GPS says turn right,
but I think it's confused.

121
00:06:21,250 --> 00:06:23,426
Morning. You lost?

122
00:06:23,513 --> 00:06:24,949
We're fine, thanks.

123
00:06:25,036 --> 00:06:27,952
[gunshots]

124
00:06:35,438 --> 00:06:38,354
[gunshots]

125
00:06:48,190 --> 00:06:49,409
Ah!

126
00:06:49,496 --> 00:06:50,410
Hang on!

127
00:06:57,765 --> 00:07:00,637
[theme music]

128
00:07:11,039 --> 00:07:13,955
[panting]

129
00:07:29,361 --> 00:07:31,668
Hey. You okay?

130
00:07:34,715 --> 00:07:36,238
Hey! Hey!

131
00:07:37,544 --> 00:07:39,763
Hey! Stop.

132
00:07:39,850 --> 00:07:41,983
Stop. I will shoot you.

133
00:07:46,248 --> 00:07:48,163
Nice driving.

134
00:07:53,734 --> 00:07:56,171
Don't waste your time.
There's no signal.

135
00:07:56,258 --> 00:07:57,868
Um..

136
00:07:57,955 --> 00:08:00,915
there was some noise over there,
like some kind of animal.

137
00:08:01,002 --> 00:08:03,352
Freaked me out.
Unlock me, okay?

138
00:08:03,439 --> 00:08:06,703
We can't stay here, and we
can't go back up to the road.

139
00:08:06,790 --> 00:08:09,140
There's too much chance
of running into that guy.

140
00:08:09,227 --> 00:08:11,142
We follow the stream
East a ways

141
00:08:11,229 --> 00:08:12,927
we'll probably run
into State Route four.

142
00:08:13,014 --> 00:08:14,711
We can catch
a cell signal there.

143
00:08:14,798 --> 00:08:16,278
I'm not going anywhere.

144
00:08:16,365 --> 00:08:17,409
It's not a choice.

145
00:08:17,497 --> 00:08:18,846
Can't make me.

146
00:08:18,933 --> 00:08:21,457
We need help.
I'm trying to protect you.

147
00:08:21,544 --> 00:08:24,634
Yeah, so I can testify
against the mob.

148
00:08:24,721 --> 00:08:27,245
Forget it.

149
00:08:27,332 --> 00:08:28,769
Okay.

150
00:08:28,856 --> 00:08:31,598
- I'll go by myself.
- Cool. Unlock me.

151
00:08:31,685 --> 00:08:35,166
I need to know where to find you
when we come back for you.

152
00:08:35,253 --> 00:08:36,907
Hey, you can't do that.

153
00:08:36,994 --> 00:08:38,779
Watch out
for rattlesnakes.

154
00:08:38,866 --> 00:08:41,259
'They're all over
through these woods.'

155
00:08:41,346 --> 00:08:43,784
Okay, wait!

156
00:08:43,871 --> 00:08:46,003
[male #1]
'I've spoken
with the forestry service.'

157
00:08:46,090 --> 00:08:47,309
They're beginning
a coordinated search

158
00:08:47,396 --> 00:08:48,963
with the sheriff's office.

159
00:08:49,050 --> 00:08:51,269
It's likely the GPS
gave Van Pelt bad directions.

160
00:08:51,356 --> 00:08:52,836
They've had people
lost this way.

161
00:08:52,923 --> 00:08:55,099
They don't think
she's gonna be hard to find.

162
00:08:55,186 --> 00:08:57,885
Get some of our people looking.
More boots on the ground.

163
00:08:57,972 --> 00:08:59,539
They're not taking
this seriously.

164
00:08:59,626 --> 00:09:01,323
How big is the area
they're searching?

165
00:09:01,410 --> 00:09:02,846
One hundred and forty
square miles.

166
00:09:02,933 --> 00:09:04,195
It sounds pretty serious.

167
00:09:04,282 --> 00:09:06,197
If you were there,
we'd look for you.

168
00:09:06,284 --> 00:09:07,851
I hope not.

169
00:09:07,938 --> 00:09:09,984
If I'm lost, I want
a search-and-rescue team

170
00:09:10,071 --> 00:09:12,464
that knows the landscape
and can cover ground fast.

171
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:15,293
Now I will make sure
every resource is devoted

172
00:09:15,380 --> 00:09:19,863
to finding Van Pelt. Okay?
Meantime, let's do our jobs.

173
00:09:22,387 --> 00:09:23,693
Boss, we need to be--

174
00:09:23,780 --> 00:09:25,652
He's right.
We don't know the terrain.

175
00:09:25,739 --> 00:09:29,003
We'll just get in the way.
Let's focus on what we cando.

176
00:09:29,090 --> 00:09:30,657
What do you got?

177
00:09:30,744 --> 00:09:34,008
Ballistics came in.
Junior was shot with a .380.

178
00:09:34,095 --> 00:09:35,792
One casing found
at the crime scene

179
00:09:35,879 --> 00:09:37,446
another, 10 yards
outside the fence.

180
00:09:37,533 --> 00:09:39,970
That must've been the shot
the killer fired at Nett

181
00:09:40,057 --> 00:09:41,450
when he was running away.

182
00:09:41,537 --> 00:09:43,887
- Any luck on the gun trace?
- No. Nothing.

183
00:09:43,974 --> 00:09:46,977
This feels like a hit to me,
like a pro at work.

184
00:09:47,064 --> 00:09:48,718
He had to have driven there.

185
00:09:48,805 --> 00:09:51,025
Let's check the gas stations
and the convenience stores

186
00:09:51,112 --> 00:09:53,810
on the road to the cabin.
Maybe he stopped off somewhere.

187
00:09:53,897 --> 00:09:55,856
Do we have anything
on the witness Janpen?

188
00:09:55,943 --> 00:09:58,380
No arrests. The other hookers
didn't have anything to say.

189
00:09:58,467 --> 00:10:00,991
I'm trying to find the pimp
that arranged the party.

190
00:10:01,078 --> 00:10:03,777
Take a hard look at
the wise guys that were there.

191
00:10:03,864 --> 00:10:06,823
If someone would know how
to hire a hit man, it's them.

192
00:10:06,910 --> 00:10:09,130
Van Pelt will be
back here in 20 minutes

193
00:10:09,217 --> 00:10:11,654
and we're all gonna
feel stupid for worrying.

194
00:10:20,315 --> 00:10:23,710
File on Porchetto Senior's
quite an interesting read.

195
00:10:23,797 --> 00:10:27,191
Murder, robbery, thuggery,
all sorts of skullduggery.

196
00:10:27,278 --> 00:10:30,107
The organized crime unit's been
after Porchetto for a while.

197
00:10:32,022 --> 00:10:33,676
There's nothing more
you can do.

198
00:10:33,763 --> 00:10:35,199
About what?

199
00:10:35,286 --> 00:10:37,071
Van Pelt. That's what
you're fretting about.

200
00:10:37,158 --> 00:10:39,334
Van Pelt is missing
because of the murder

201
00:10:39,421 --> 00:10:41,771
ergo, we focus on
catching the murderer

202
00:10:41,858 --> 00:10:43,643
chances are
we'll find Van Pelt..

203
00:10:43,730 --> 00:10:45,949
unless someone else
finds her first, but right now?

204
00:10:46,036 --> 00:10:47,516
Let's go. Porchettos.

205
00:10:54,610 --> 00:10:56,656
Agent Lisbon. Mr. Jane.

206
00:10:56,743 --> 00:10:58,266
Andrew Kellogg.
I'm the Porchettos' attorney.

207
00:10:58,353 --> 00:11:00,747
This is Iris Porchetto,
Gabe's stepmother.

208
00:11:00,834 --> 00:11:02,313
Where is Mr. Porchetto?

209
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:04,098
On his way.
He's not feeling well.

210
00:11:04,185 --> 00:11:05,621
We'll have to
keep this brief.

211
00:11:05,708 --> 00:11:06,970
We'll have to be thorough

212
00:11:07,057 --> 00:11:08,798
but I'll keep
your concerns in mind.

213
00:11:08,885 --> 00:11:11,148
Let's play cards up, agent.

214
00:11:11,235 --> 00:11:14,195
The police have unjustly hounded
the Porchettos for years.

215
00:11:14,282 --> 00:11:16,545
I will not stand
for that sort of thing.

216
00:11:16,632 --> 00:11:18,329
'These the cops?'

217
00:11:18,416 --> 00:11:20,767
[Lisbon]
We're with the CBI,
Mr. Porchetto.

218
00:11:20,854 --> 00:11:24,422
This is who they send
to find my boy's killer?

219
00:11:24,509 --> 00:11:26,511
A girl and a guy in a vest.

220
00:11:26,598 --> 00:11:28,644
This is really a waste
of my time.

221
00:11:28,731 --> 00:11:30,777
- I want a drink.
- No.

222
00:11:30,864 --> 00:11:32,866
Gabe is dead.
I can have a drink.

223
00:11:32,953 --> 00:11:35,520
Not with your meds.
It's got bad interaction.

224
00:11:35,607 --> 00:11:37,958
Uh, excuse me.
Where is the cancer?

225
00:11:38,045 --> 00:11:39,611
What's your name?

226
00:11:39,699 --> 00:11:42,092
Jane. Patrick Jane.

227
00:11:42,179 --> 00:11:44,094
Liver? Kidney? Spleen?

228
00:11:44,181 --> 00:11:45,356
Kidney.

229
00:11:45,443 --> 00:11:47,707
Oh. How long
did they give you?

230
00:11:47,794 --> 00:11:50,405
"How long"? I'm a dead man.
That's how long.

231
00:11:50,492 --> 00:11:52,494
Having trouble sleeping,
I expect.

232
00:11:52,581 --> 00:11:55,018
Yes. Why?

233
00:11:55,105 --> 00:11:57,629
Well, I can tell you
how to get to sleep

234
00:11:57,717 --> 00:12:00,328
if you tell us
who you think killed your son.

235
00:12:00,415 --> 00:12:02,069
Who says I know?

236
00:12:02,156 --> 00:12:04,332
You said you were
wasting your time with us

237
00:12:04,419 --> 00:12:06,595
so I assumed you already knew
who was responsible.

238
00:12:06,682 --> 00:12:08,336
Do you, Mr. Porchetto?

239
00:12:08,423 --> 00:12:10,294
- Don't say anything.
- Honey, listen to Andrew.

240
00:12:10,381 --> 00:12:12,819
This one can't wait
to put me in the ground.

241
00:12:12,906 --> 00:12:14,168
That's not true.

242
00:12:14,255 --> 00:12:16,170
That's not true.

243
00:12:16,257 --> 00:12:18,346
Maybe just a little true?

244
00:12:18,433 --> 00:12:21,349
You want me
to do your job? Fine.

245
00:12:21,436 --> 00:12:23,177
It was the Mexicans.

246
00:12:23,264 --> 00:12:24,569
What Mexicans?

247
00:12:24,656 --> 00:12:26,920
Julio Iglesias.
Who do you think?

248
00:12:27,007 --> 00:12:29,792
The Zetas.
The Zetas.

249
00:12:29,879 --> 00:12:31,794
- The Mexican drug cartel?
- Yeah.

250
00:12:31,881 --> 00:12:33,883
Why would they want
to kill your son?

251
00:12:33,970 --> 00:12:37,626
I'm not saying any more.
About that sleeping trick..

252
00:12:37,713 --> 00:12:40,324
Oh, yes.
When you breathe in, count one.

253
00:12:40,411 --> 00:12:45,373
When you breathe out, count two.
In one, out two. Very simple.

254
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:49,246
Think of nothing else, except
your breath and those numbers.

255
00:12:49,333 --> 00:12:51,466
And that will make me sleep?

256
00:12:51,553 --> 00:12:54,338
Like a big, murderous baby.

257
00:12:54,425 --> 00:12:56,079
Ciao.

258
00:12:59,169 --> 00:13:01,476
Organized crime unit says
Junior wanted the Porchettos

259
00:13:01,563 --> 00:13:03,043
to sell meth in the Northeast.

260
00:13:03,130 --> 00:13:05,349
The Zetas control the drug trade
in that territory.

261
00:13:05,436 --> 00:13:07,874
If junior did make a move,
they could've killed him.

262
00:13:07,961 --> 00:13:09,571
Call Bernie Westeroff
in narcotics.

263
00:13:09,658 --> 00:13:13,227
See if he has a line on any
Zeta foot soldiers in the area.

264
00:13:13,314 --> 00:13:16,099
You're gonna get
a Mexican drug dealer to talk?

265
00:13:16,186 --> 00:13:18,058
- I'll think of something.
- Ohh.

266
00:13:19,711 --> 00:13:21,670
Wayne.

267
00:13:21,757 --> 00:13:23,106
Sarah.

268
00:13:23,193 --> 00:13:24,891
Yeah, I was looking for you.
Lunch.

269
00:13:24,978 --> 00:13:26,588
Oh. Damn. I forgot.

270
00:13:26,675 --> 00:13:27,981
[sighs]

271
00:13:28,068 --> 00:13:30,026
No, look, I'm sorry.
Grace is missing.

272
00:13:30,113 --> 00:13:31,854
Oh, my lord.
What's happened?

273
00:13:31,941 --> 00:13:35,031
We-we don't know. Look,
she was in a state park and..

274
00:13:35,118 --> 00:13:37,338
anyway, I have to work.
I'm sorry.

275
00:13:37,425 --> 00:13:39,906
Of course. You work.
We'll just do it another time.

276
00:13:39,993 --> 00:13:41,472
Yeah. Just call me
later, okay?

277
00:13:41,559 --> 00:13:43,213
And I'm sure it's fine.
She's fine.

278
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:45,085
Thanks.

279
00:14:00,622 --> 00:14:02,493
Um..

280
00:14:02,580 --> 00:14:04,582
It's really hard
to walk like this.

281
00:14:04,669 --> 00:14:07,150
Should have thought of that
before you ran.

282
00:14:10,458 --> 00:14:11,807
[rustle]

283
00:14:12,503 --> 00:14:14,941
Stay here.

284
00:14:15,028 --> 00:14:16,333
[rustle]

285
00:14:26,735 --> 00:14:29,303
[rustle]

286
00:14:36,527 --> 00:14:39,095
[wings flapping]

287
00:14:39,182 --> 00:14:41,315
'Hey, Grace.'

288
00:14:41,402 --> 00:14:43,143
[pants]

289
00:14:48,191 --> 00:14:50,454
- Who are you?
- Come on, Grace.

290
00:14:50,541 --> 00:14:51,847
Craig's dead. I killed him.

291
00:14:51,934 --> 00:14:54,415
Yeah. Yeah, you did that.

292
00:14:54,502 --> 00:14:56,156
Are you a ghost?

293
00:14:56,243 --> 00:14:58,201
What do you think?

294
00:15:01,291 --> 00:15:03,250
If you're not a ghost,
what are you?

295
00:15:03,337 --> 00:15:05,295
Grace, look, you've been
in a car accident.

296
00:15:05,382 --> 00:15:07,907
You're dehydrated,
pumped on adrenaline.

297
00:15:07,994 --> 00:15:09,909
Maybe I'm just
something you're seeing.

298
00:15:10,997 --> 00:15:13,825
The question is, why now?

299
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:16,263
Why do you need
to see me, Grace?

300
00:15:16,350 --> 00:15:18,265
[Janpen]
'Hey!'

301
00:15:18,352 --> 00:15:21,181
What's going on?

302
00:15:21,268 --> 00:15:23,661
Nothing. Let's keep walking.

303
00:15:33,236 --> 00:15:35,847
Hey, Lisbon.

304
00:15:35,935 --> 00:15:37,458
What'd you get
for me, Bernie?

305
00:15:37,545 --> 00:15:40,374
You wanted a Zeta,
I got you one. Luis Osorio.

306
00:15:40,461 --> 00:15:42,463
A lieutenant, connected,
should know stuff.

307
00:15:42,550 --> 00:15:44,900
- I owe you one. Thanks.
- Yeah, maybe not.

308
00:15:44,987 --> 00:15:47,990
The charge I got Osorio on
is bogus, and he knows it

309
00:15:48,077 --> 00:15:51,298
so he'll keep his mouth shut.
His lawyer gets here, he walks.

310
00:15:51,385 --> 00:15:52,864
I like my chances.

311
00:16:00,133 --> 00:16:03,136
Hi, Mr. Osorio.
Uh, Patrick Jane.

312
00:16:03,223 --> 00:16:05,225
'Sorry we've kept you so long.'

313
00:16:05,312 --> 00:16:08,141
Promise we won't
keep you much longer.

314
00:16:08,228 --> 00:16:09,969
[sighs]

315
00:16:10,056 --> 00:16:12,580
You play cards?

316
00:16:12,667 --> 00:16:15,017
'Want to play a little game?'

317
00:16:15,104 --> 00:16:18,542
It's find the queen. Alright?

318
00:16:18,629 --> 00:16:22,894
There she is there.
All you have to do is find her.

319
00:16:22,982 --> 00:16:26,028
You follow the queen, you keep
an eye on where she goes

320
00:16:26,115 --> 00:16:29,466
and then you bet.
There. Not here. There she is.

321
00:16:29,553 --> 00:16:32,078
[cards clack]

322
00:16:32,165 --> 00:16:33,993
Where is she?

323
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:37,083
I don't give a damn
where she is.

324
00:16:37,170 --> 00:16:38,649
[Patrick]
Hmm.

325
00:16:38,736 --> 00:16:40,738
What do you think I am?
A child?

326
00:16:40,825 --> 00:16:43,698
Excuse me. I was just trying
to kill a little time.

327
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:48,485
[clacking]

328
00:16:50,226 --> 00:16:52,402
- Where is she?
- 'She's on the right.'

329
00:16:56,885 --> 00:16:59,844
- Hmm. How you do that?
- The hype.

330
00:16:59,931 --> 00:17:03,500
You pick up two cards
between your fingers like so

331
00:17:03,587 --> 00:17:05,111
but when you throw down

332
00:17:05,198 --> 00:17:07,852
it appears that you throw
the bottom card

333
00:17:07,939 --> 00:17:09,941
when in fact,
you throw the top card..

334
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:14,511
Like that. See how that looked
like it was the bottom card?

335
00:17:14,598 --> 00:17:16,470
Huh. Nice.

336
00:17:16,557 --> 00:17:19,908
You hold it like that, you just
drop it down there like that.

337
00:17:19,995 --> 00:17:23,085
'It's very easy.
Lot of practice.'

338
00:17:23,172 --> 00:17:25,870
It's fun to watch, when you
know what's happening, isn't it?

339
00:17:25,957 --> 00:17:28,917
Kind of relaxing. Soothing.

340
00:17:30,353 --> 00:17:32,138
[cards clacking]

341
00:17:32,225 --> 00:17:34,966
Tell me something.

342
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:37,491
You think the Zetas
killed Gabriel Porchetto?

343
00:17:37,578 --> 00:17:41,016
Nah. Zetas didn't have
any reason to kill him.

344
00:17:41,103 --> 00:17:43,453
Not yet, anyhow.

345
00:17:43,540 --> 00:17:45,542
Man was all talk.

346
00:17:45,629 --> 00:17:47,370
Good to know.

347
00:17:47,457 --> 00:17:49,329
Alright, you try.

348
00:17:51,418 --> 00:17:52,680
'Go ahead.'

349
00:17:54,247 --> 00:17:55,683
[rustle]

350
00:17:55,770 --> 00:17:57,250
Look at you.
You're a natural.

351
00:17:57,337 --> 00:17:59,426
Look at the way
you hold those cards.

352
00:17:59,513 --> 00:18:03,256
'And you drop the first one
down, just like that.'

353
00:18:03,343 --> 00:18:04,953
Two hands, let it flop.

354
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:07,651
That's a beginning,
that's a start. Baby steps.

355
00:18:09,566 --> 00:18:11,829
Who do you think
killed Porchetto?

356
00:18:11,916 --> 00:18:14,658
Well, people say, uh..

357
00:18:14,745 --> 00:18:18,532
...he got into a fight
with a biker..

358
00:18:18,619 --> 00:18:21,448
biker named Wood. Ha.

359
00:18:21,535 --> 00:18:24,190
Almost have it. Almost.

360
00:18:24,277 --> 00:18:26,453
You can swindle people
before you behead them

361
00:18:26,540 --> 00:18:30,631
or whatever it is
you do to them.

362
00:18:30,718 --> 00:18:33,068
I never beheaded nobody.

363
00:18:33,155 --> 00:18:35,723
Slit a few throats maybe.

364
00:18:35,810 --> 00:18:38,856
Okay. Zero beheadings.

365
00:18:38,943 --> 00:18:40,771
Hmm.

366
00:18:40,858 --> 00:18:42,512
[Cho]
'Ran the biker named Wood.'

367
00:18:42,599 --> 00:18:45,167
There's an incident report
on a bar fight Junior had

368
00:18:45,254 --> 00:18:47,735
with a gang member named
Elwood Spiller two weeks ago.

369
00:18:47,822 --> 00:18:49,650
No arrest. Spiller refused
to press charges.

370
00:18:49,737 --> 00:18:52,174
- Find out what it was about.
- Boss, check this out.

371
00:18:52,261 --> 00:18:54,263
Nothing from the gas stations
in the area

372
00:18:54,350 --> 00:18:56,787
but I found some video cameras
near the crime scene

373
00:18:56,874 --> 00:18:58,354
some professor studying
animal migration patterns.

374
00:18:58,441 --> 00:19:01,227
One of them caught a white male
driving near the cabin

375
00:19:01,314 --> 00:19:02,402
right after the shooting.

376
00:19:02,489 --> 00:19:03,925
Did they get the plate?

377
00:19:04,012 --> 00:19:06,319
'No, but we were able
to enhance the image.'

378
00:19:06,406 --> 00:19:08,582
Asked the FBI to run it
through facial recognition

379
00:19:08,669 --> 00:19:10,888
and this one
seemed like the best shot.

380
00:19:10,975 --> 00:19:13,674
Raynor Marquette. He's from L.A.
He's got a long sheet.

381
00:19:13,761 --> 00:19:15,458
FBI thinks
he runs guns into Tijuana

382
00:19:15,545 --> 00:19:17,243
and that
he's a killer for hire.

383
00:19:17,330 --> 00:19:19,332
See if you can find out
anything else

384
00:19:19,419 --> 00:19:21,595
and send that picture
to the county sheriff's office.

385
00:19:21,682 --> 00:19:24,075
Okay. Hey.
You, uh, hear anything?

386
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:27,122
They've covered 40%
of the search area. Nothing yet.

387
00:19:29,516 --> 00:19:30,473
[water trickling]

388
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:32,040
So where are you from?

389
00:19:32,127 --> 00:19:33,476
Barstow.

390
00:19:33,563 --> 00:19:35,609
A cousin of my mom's
raised me.

391
00:19:35,696 --> 00:19:38,220
Meth head. Not so great
with the mother thing.

392
00:19:38,307 --> 00:19:40,527
She got me started
in this massage parlor.

393
00:19:40,614 --> 00:19:43,573
I was, like, 11, maybe.

394
00:19:45,749 --> 00:19:48,099
I wasn't the youngest.

395
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:50,276
Anyways,
a couple years after

396
00:19:50,363 --> 00:19:52,495
this Guatemalan arms dealer
bought me..

397
00:19:52,582 --> 00:19:55,585
...and I was, like, his pet.

398
00:19:56,891 --> 00:19:58,675
And that was
kind of weird.

399
00:19:58,762 --> 00:20:02,984
And then he got k..
Ow!

400
00:20:03,071 --> 00:20:05,029
- Are you okay?
- No!

401
00:20:05,116 --> 00:20:07,206
Bitch, take these off.

402
00:20:08,816 --> 00:20:11,079
Like I'm gonna run. Where?

403
00:20:11,166 --> 00:20:13,124
I have no idea where we are

404
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:15,649
or how to get to where
you say we're going.

405
00:20:15,736 --> 00:20:18,129
'Last thing I'm gonna do
is take off.'

406
00:20:23,309 --> 00:20:24,484
Alright.

407
00:20:24,571 --> 00:20:25,789
Thank you.

408
00:20:25,876 --> 00:20:27,922
It'll be dark soon.

409
00:20:28,009 --> 00:20:30,490
We need to find a place
to spend the night.

410
00:20:30,577 --> 00:20:33,144
Um..

411
00:20:33,232 --> 00:20:36,409
Shouldn't there be people out
looking for us? Where arethey?

412
00:20:36,496 --> 00:20:39,020
I don't know. Come on.

413
00:20:39,107 --> 00:20:40,630
Come on.

414
00:20:43,807 --> 00:20:46,680
[whirring]

415
00:20:56,559 --> 00:20:59,258
Elwood Spiller.
Kimball Cho, CBI.

416
00:20:59,345 --> 00:21:01,303
I want to talk
about Junior Porchetto.

417
00:21:01,390 --> 00:21:03,784
Did you and he
have a fight on the 17th?

418
00:21:03,871 --> 00:21:05,525
No, we did not.

419
00:21:05,612 --> 00:21:07,048
Well, according to
the incident report

420
00:21:07,135 --> 00:21:08,832
you got into an argument
with Junior

421
00:21:08,919 --> 00:21:11,922
and he had three of his guys
beat you to a pulp.

422
00:21:12,009 --> 00:21:13,837
- Nope.
- Well, how'd all this happen?

423
00:21:13,924 --> 00:21:17,101
- A boating accident.
- Now junior did this to you.

424
00:21:17,188 --> 00:21:18,886
Now you must have
a major grudge.

425
00:21:18,973 --> 00:21:21,715
We can talk about it here,
or I'll take you in

426
00:21:21,802 --> 00:21:24,457
you can sit in a cell
and talk about it tomorrow.

427
00:21:24,544 --> 00:21:26,676
Old man Porchetto
is on a hunt.

428
00:21:26,763 --> 00:21:30,201
Anybody he thinks had anything
to do with hitting Junior

429
00:21:30,289 --> 00:21:31,681
is gonna get clipped.

430
00:21:31,768 --> 00:21:36,207
So you can take me
wherever you'd like.

431
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:38,906
All I'm saying

432
00:21:38,993 --> 00:21:41,996
is Junior Porchetto
was one hell of a guy

433
00:21:42,083 --> 00:21:44,172
and he always
treated me good.

434
00:21:45,826 --> 00:21:47,567
[sighs]

435
00:21:50,918 --> 00:21:53,573
You do know
his old man is sick, right?

436
00:21:54,530 --> 00:21:58,142
When he dies, come back.

437
00:21:58,229 --> 00:22:00,057
I might say
something different.

438
00:22:00,144 --> 00:22:02,669
Interesting.

439
00:22:02,756 --> 00:22:05,454
He said, come back
after the father's dead.

440
00:22:05,541 --> 00:22:07,064
That's right.

441
00:22:07,151 --> 00:22:08,414
That's interesting.

442
00:22:08,501 --> 00:22:10,981
We know killing Junior
was a major play.

443
00:22:11,068 --> 00:22:12,766
Whoever did it
took a big risk.

444
00:22:12,853 --> 00:22:14,594
Must've expected a big payoff.
Who's that?

445
00:22:14,681 --> 00:22:16,857
Hard to say. According to
the organized crime unit

446
00:22:16,944 --> 00:22:18,902
the main person who benefits
from Junior's death

447
00:22:18,989 --> 00:22:20,513
- is old man Porchetto himself.
- Why?

448
00:22:20,600 --> 00:22:22,602
Well, if they moved in
after Zeta territory

449
00:22:22,689 --> 00:22:25,126
the way that Junior wanted,
they would've started a war.

450
00:22:25,213 --> 00:22:26,432
Could've ended
the Porchetto organization.

451
00:22:26,519 --> 00:22:28,434
Junior was getting in
way over his head.

452
00:22:28,521 --> 00:22:31,001
[cell phone rings]

453
00:22:31,088 --> 00:22:34,265
It's the sheriff's office.
Lisbon.

454
00:22:36,746 --> 00:22:38,618
Okay, thank you.

455
00:22:38,705 --> 00:22:40,446
They're suspending the search
for the night.

456
00:22:40,533 --> 00:22:42,230
They're gonna start again
in the morning.

457
00:22:42,317 --> 00:22:43,449
They're doing something wrong.

458
00:22:43,536 --> 00:22:45,451
They should've
found her by now.

459
00:22:45,538 --> 00:22:48,541
They're doing something wrong.

460
00:22:48,628 --> 00:22:50,499
Um, either of you play squash?

461
00:22:50,586 --> 00:22:51,979
[Lisbon]
'What?'

462
00:22:52,066 --> 00:22:53,110
You know, squash.

463
00:22:53,197 --> 00:22:55,809
- No.
- No.

464
00:22:55,896 --> 00:22:59,508
I need a squash ball.

465
00:22:59,595 --> 00:23:01,249
It's about that big
little, black thing.

466
00:23:01,336 --> 00:23:03,251
Doesn't bounce very well.

467
00:23:13,043 --> 00:23:16,786
I know what you want to ask.
Don't be embarrassed.

468
00:23:16,873 --> 00:23:19,876
I am not talking to you.

469
00:23:19,963 --> 00:23:23,706
You are just a figment
of my imagination.

470
00:23:23,793 --> 00:23:25,839
Please yourself.

471
00:23:31,540 --> 00:23:34,064
Did you love me?

472
00:23:34,151 --> 00:23:35,370
Of course I loved you.

473
00:23:35,457 --> 00:23:38,417
Then why did you
try to kill me?

474
00:23:38,504 --> 00:23:41,463
I had to make a choice
between you and Red John.

475
00:23:41,550 --> 00:23:43,596
We all have to make
hard choices, Grace

476
00:23:43,683 --> 00:23:45,815
Doesn't make me evil.

477
00:23:45,902 --> 00:23:47,426
[scoffs]
Kind of does.

478
00:23:47,513 --> 00:23:48,644
Grace

479
00:23:48,731 --> 00:23:51,038
I was just too stupid
to see it.

480
00:23:51,125 --> 00:23:53,083
- Oh, no, you saw it.
- No, I didn't.

481
00:23:53,170 --> 00:23:55,651
Not all of it, but you knew
there was something..

482
00:23:55,738 --> 00:23:59,176
something a little dangerous
under the nice guy stuff.

483
00:23:59,263 --> 00:24:02,266
You kind of liked it.

484
00:24:02,353 --> 00:24:04,312
You can't open your eyes
a little bit.

485
00:24:04,399 --> 00:24:07,358
Gotta open 'em all the way
if you wanna see the truth.

486
00:24:07,446 --> 00:24:10,318
What are you talking about?

487
00:24:10,405 --> 00:24:14,017
Why are you doing this
to me?

488
00:24:14,104 --> 00:24:16,585
How should I know?

489
00:24:16,672 --> 00:24:20,371
I'm just a figment
of your imagination.

490
00:24:56,582 --> 00:24:58,497
Damn it.

491
00:24:59,672 --> 00:25:01,108
[whispers]
Hey.

492
00:25:01,195 --> 00:25:02,849
Did you find
your squash ball?

493
00:25:02,936 --> 00:25:06,243
Oh, yes, I did,
as a matter of fact. Thank you.

494
00:25:06,330 --> 00:25:07,984
Um, I'm headed over
to the Porchettos.

495
00:25:08,071 --> 00:25:09,290
Why?

496
00:25:09,377 --> 00:25:11,510
It probably won't work,
but if it does

497
00:25:11,597 --> 00:25:15,905
you're gonna have to move fast,
so stay on your toes.

498
00:25:15,992 --> 00:25:17,820
Boss. They're looking
in the wrong place.

499
00:25:17,907 --> 00:25:19,953
- What do you mean?
- The searchers messed up.

500
00:25:20,040 --> 00:25:21,520
That's why they haven't
found anything.

501
00:25:21,607 --> 00:25:24,044
They started the search
at the last cell phone tower

502
00:25:24,131 --> 00:25:25,872
that Van Pelt's phone
made contact with.

503
00:25:25,959 --> 00:25:28,657
They figured she was within
a 15-mile radius of this point.

504
00:25:28,744 --> 00:25:30,703
- That makes sense.
- But they're wrong. I checked.

505
00:25:30,790 --> 00:25:33,009
The next tower, here, was down
for maintenance yesterday.

506
00:25:33,096 --> 00:25:35,490
If her phone tried to make
contact with thistower

507
00:25:35,577 --> 00:25:36,752
there'd be no record.

508
00:25:36,839 --> 00:25:38,537
They should be looking
10 miles further.

509
00:25:38,624 --> 00:25:39,799
I'm going out there.

510
00:25:39,886 --> 00:25:42,497
You go.
I'll deal with Wainwright.

511
00:25:42,584 --> 00:25:46,457
[cell phone rings]

512
00:25:46,545 --> 00:25:47,589
Hey, sir.

513
00:25:47,676 --> 00:25:50,418
Wayne, hi.
Um, I know you're busy.

514
00:25:50,505 --> 00:25:52,768
I was just wondering
how things are.

515
00:25:52,855 --> 00:25:55,510
We still haven't found her
yet. I'm heading out there.

516
00:25:55,597 --> 00:25:58,818
Um, well, I just want you to
know I was thinking about you

517
00:25:58,905 --> 00:26:01,124
and praying for Grace,
and..

518
00:26:01,211 --> 00:26:04,388
I just know that this is
gonna turn out alright.

519
00:26:04,475 --> 00:26:05,955
Thanks.
Listen, I have to go.

520
00:26:06,042 --> 00:26:09,350
The, uh, elevator's here.
I'll call you later, yeah?

521
00:26:12,005 --> 00:26:13,920
Janpen?!

522
00:26:14,007 --> 00:26:16,226
Janpen?!

523
00:26:16,313 --> 00:26:17,663
Don't blame yourself.

524
00:26:17,750 --> 00:26:18,751
I fell asleep.

525
00:26:18,838 --> 00:26:20,230
Yeah. You were tired.

526
00:26:20,317 --> 00:26:21,797
She gets lost,
she could die.

527
00:26:21,884 --> 00:26:23,843
Why did I think
I could stay awake?

528
00:26:23,930 --> 00:26:24,887
Everything isn't your fault.

529
00:26:24,974 --> 00:26:26,280
This is my fault.

530
00:26:26,367 --> 00:26:28,108
- I wasn't your fault.
- Yes, you were.

531
00:26:28,195 --> 00:26:31,372
You were with me when you killed
those cops and you shot Lisbon.

532
00:26:31,459 --> 00:26:33,113
I should have stopped you.

533
00:26:33,200 --> 00:26:35,855
You did.
You killed me.

534
00:26:35,942 --> 00:26:37,552
I was too late.

535
00:26:37,639 --> 00:26:40,773
I should have seen it sooner.
I should have done something.

536
00:26:40,860 --> 00:26:44,124
How? You were in love with me.
Don't you remember?

537
00:26:48,476 --> 00:26:51,871
There she is.

538
00:26:54,177 --> 00:26:57,180
- Where'd you go?
- I had to pee.

539
00:26:57,267 --> 00:26:59,922
Who were you talking to?

540
00:27:00,009 --> 00:27:02,142
- Nobody.
- Great.

541
00:27:02,229 --> 00:27:04,535
Lost in the woods
with a crazy cop.

542
00:27:04,623 --> 00:27:06,102
Hey, I got it worse.

543
00:27:06,189 --> 00:27:09,540
I'm lost in the woods
with a grumpy hooker. Let's go.

544
00:27:16,591 --> 00:27:20,900
The silent intimidation act
is quite effective.

545
00:27:20,987 --> 00:27:23,032
I'll admit, I'm intimidated.

546
00:27:23,119 --> 00:27:25,339
Then he forced himself in here,
and won't leave.

547
00:27:25,426 --> 00:27:27,863
- You have to do something--
- Iris. You need to relax.

548
00:27:27,950 --> 00:27:29,212
Tension causes wrinkles.

549
00:27:29,299 --> 00:27:31,040
Mr. Jane,
what are you doing here?

550
00:27:31,127 --> 00:27:33,782
- I need to speak to Porchetto.
- You can't talk to him.

551
00:27:33,869 --> 00:27:35,566
Yes, I can.

552
00:27:35,654 --> 00:27:37,612
Do you see what I mean?
This is...

553
00:27:37,699 --> 00:27:41,137
If you don't leave,
I'll protest to your superiors.

554
00:27:41,224 --> 00:27:43,009
You can't harass my client
like this.

555
00:27:43,096 --> 00:27:45,881
How long have you two been
carrying on this affair?

556
00:27:45,968 --> 00:27:47,491
What do you mean?

557
00:27:47,578 --> 00:27:50,016
Your protectiveness of Iris
is more than legal

558
00:27:50,103 --> 00:27:53,715
and she keeps touching your
elbow. Hard to misinterpret.

559
00:27:53,802 --> 00:27:55,978
I'm pretty sure
Curtis here already knows.

560
00:27:56,065 --> 00:27:58,894
Yes, he looks dense,
but he's as sharp as a tack.

561
00:27:58,981 --> 00:28:01,941
Doesn't miss a beat,
do you, Curtis?

562
00:28:02,028 --> 00:28:04,900
This is...
completely irrelevant.

563
00:28:04,987 --> 00:28:06,902
Are you worried
that Porchetto's gonna find out

564
00:28:06,989 --> 00:28:08,817
or does it add
a more excitement?

565
00:28:08,904 --> 00:28:11,341
- Did you just threaten us?
- Let's take a breath here.

566
00:28:11,428 --> 00:28:13,387
[Porchetto]
'What's going on?'

567
00:28:13,474 --> 00:28:14,562
You.

568
00:28:14,649 --> 00:28:16,346
Well, good morning.

569
00:28:16,433 --> 00:28:20,350
That trick, one two, one two...
damned if it doesn't work.

570
00:28:20,437 --> 00:28:23,136
- Fell asleep in no time.
- Glad to hear it.

571
00:28:23,223 --> 00:28:25,268
What do you want?

572
00:28:25,355 --> 00:28:27,618
Do you think we could
talk someplace else?

573
00:28:27,706 --> 00:28:30,970
It's kind of
a private matter.

574
00:28:40,196 --> 00:28:43,460
So what is it?

575
00:28:44,853 --> 00:28:47,290
Well, colleague of mine
is missing.

576
00:28:47,377 --> 00:28:49,597
I think it's connected
to your son's murder.

577
00:28:49,684 --> 00:28:51,425
You're still looking
for the murderer, right?

578
00:28:51,512 --> 00:28:52,774
Maybe.

579
00:28:52,861 --> 00:28:54,863
Sure you are.
You want to kill him.

580
00:28:54,950 --> 00:28:56,517
I get it, believe me.

581
00:28:56,604 --> 00:29:00,260
But have you found him?
'Cause I'd like to talk to him

582
00:29:00,347 --> 00:29:03,306
Then you can have him back,
Do whatever you want with him.

583
00:29:03,393 --> 00:29:04,873
I don't know
anything about it.

584
00:29:04,960 --> 00:29:06,440
- Are you sure?
- Yeah, I'm sure.

585
00:29:06,527 --> 00:29:08,268
Crap.

586
00:29:08,355 --> 00:29:10,052
You were my last hope.

587
00:29:10,139 --> 00:29:14,187
Okay. What do I do now?
I could use a drink. Um...

588
00:29:16,189 --> 00:29:18,147
You don't have any vodka,
do you?

589
00:29:18,234 --> 00:29:21,237
I can't have booze around.
My meds.

590
00:29:21,324 --> 00:29:22,543
Surely, you got a stash.

591
00:29:22,630 --> 00:29:24,588
A man like you
would have a stash.

592
00:29:24,675 --> 00:29:26,982
I only want a nip, just..
Maybe two.

593
00:29:27,069 --> 00:29:29,811
Really craving that
warm, comforting feeling

594
00:29:29,898 --> 00:29:31,900
of alcohol hitting
the back of your throat.

595
00:29:31,987 --> 00:29:36,513
You know.
It just levels me.

596
00:29:36,600 --> 00:29:38,907
Uh, don't tell my wife.

597
00:29:54,227 --> 00:29:57,404
Mm. Love that sound.

598
00:29:59,319 --> 00:30:01,321
You're a saint.
Thank you.

599
00:30:01,408 --> 00:30:03,323
[sniffs and sighs]

600
00:30:03,410 --> 00:30:06,587
Mmm.

601
00:30:06,674 --> 00:30:09,285
Mmm.

602
00:30:09,982 --> 00:30:12,854
Mmm.

603
00:30:12,941 --> 00:30:15,030
[sighs]

604
00:30:15,117 --> 00:30:17,816
Yep, that's it.
Just levels me.

605
00:30:17,903 --> 00:30:20,601
It's like an angel
crying on your tongue.

606
00:30:20,688 --> 00:30:22,168
[sighs]

607
00:30:22,255 --> 00:30:23,778
That's good.

608
00:30:23,865 --> 00:30:25,867
You?

609
00:30:25,954 --> 00:30:28,696
Doctors say it messes me up.

610
00:30:28,783 --> 00:30:32,004
Oh, them. Doctors.
Always with the rules.

611
00:30:32,091 --> 00:30:35,268
I mean, as if they know
anything for sure.

612
00:30:36,269 --> 00:30:37,923
One.

613
00:30:40,839 --> 00:30:42,579
[pours vodka]

614
00:30:48,977 --> 00:30:50,674
Ah.

615
00:30:52,024 --> 00:30:53,852
[exhales deeply]

616
00:30:53,939 --> 00:30:56,419
So Mike has a...

617
00:30:56,506 --> 00:30:59,640
pool cue, and, uh...

618
00:30:59,727 --> 00:31:01,207
Cheers.
[glasses clink]

619
00:31:01,294 --> 00:31:04,775
Cheers. And sammy's
right behind me..

620
00:31:04,863 --> 00:31:07,517
and, uh..

621
00:31:07,604 --> 00:31:09,737
and I have a shovel.
He says...

622
00:31:09,824 --> 00:31:11,608
[grunts]

623
00:31:11,695 --> 00:31:13,001
[glass clinks]

624
00:31:22,445 --> 00:31:24,970
Man down! Man down in here!

625
00:31:25,057 --> 00:31:26,841
What the hell happened?

626
00:31:26,928 --> 00:31:28,799
He just fell off.
I don't know.

627
00:31:28,887 --> 00:31:31,672
Does he have a pulse?
Check.

628
00:31:31,759 --> 00:31:33,108
I don't feel anything.

629
00:31:33,195 --> 00:31:34,675
- Let me check.
- Oh, my God.

630
00:31:34,762 --> 00:31:37,504
Is he breathing? I can't
tell if he's breathing.

631
00:31:37,591 --> 00:31:40,072
- I'm not getting a pulse.
- I don't think he's breathing.

632
00:31:40,159 --> 00:31:42,509
Is this it? Is this happening?
Oh, my God.

633
00:31:42,596 --> 00:31:45,381
- Someone call an ambulance!
- I'll call right now.

634
00:31:45,468 --> 00:31:47,470
What should we do?
We should do something.

635
00:31:47,557 --> 00:31:49,037
I'll get the guys.

636
00:31:49,124 --> 00:31:51,344
We can't just leave him here.
It's so undignified.

637
00:31:51,431 --> 00:31:53,650
Do you have somewhere
you can lay him down?

638
00:31:53,737 --> 00:31:56,088
- 'In the front room.'
- Front room it is, then.

639
00:31:56,175 --> 00:31:58,699
- Guys. Come on, come on!
- I need a hand here.

640
00:32:20,155 --> 00:32:21,548
Porchetto's dead?

641
00:32:21,635 --> 00:32:22,941
Oh, more like drunk.

642
00:32:23,028 --> 00:32:24,116
Are you drunk?

643
00:32:24,203 --> 00:32:25,769
A little.
Let's not get distracted.

644
00:32:25,856 --> 00:32:27,815
[whispers]
I think someone is
staging a coup

645
00:32:27,902 --> 00:32:29,686
inside the Porchetto family

646
00:32:29,773 --> 00:32:31,688
a takeover
when the old man dies.

647
00:32:31,775 --> 00:32:33,386
- That's who killed Junior.
- Why?

648
00:32:33,473 --> 00:32:36,084
Because Junior wanted
to go to war with the zetas--

649
00:32:36,171 --> 00:32:37,999
would have destroyed
the family

650
00:32:38,086 --> 00:32:39,653
before the plotter
could take over.

651
00:32:39,740 --> 00:32:42,177
So you're trying to get
the plotter to reveal himself

652
00:32:42,264 --> 00:32:44,310
by pretending
that Porchetto's dead?

653
00:32:44,397 --> 00:32:46,355
Oh, you're very good,
grasshopper.

654
00:32:46,442 --> 00:32:48,401
Won't the doctors
figure out he's not dead?

655
00:32:48,488 --> 00:32:51,186
They're figuring it out now.
so we have to work fast.

656
00:32:51,273 --> 00:32:52,492
But Van Pelt is missing.

657
00:32:52,579 --> 00:32:53,972
- Excuse me, doctor?
- Yes.

658
00:32:54,059 --> 00:32:56,017
My name's Patrick Jane.
I'm with the CBI.

659
00:32:56,104 --> 00:32:58,106
Do you take bribe money
from big pharma?

660
00:32:58,193 --> 00:33:00,979
What?

661
00:33:01,066 --> 00:33:03,677
That's an offensive suggestion.
Why would you say that?

662
00:33:03,764 --> 00:33:04,983
Well, a lot of doctors...

663
00:33:05,070 --> 00:33:08,421
what's he saying?

664
00:33:08,508 --> 00:33:11,424
I mean, obviously,
in any profession

665
00:33:11,511 --> 00:33:14,905
people fall short
of the ethical mark.

666
00:33:14,993 --> 00:33:16,733
What's that doctor
saying to the cop?

667
00:33:16,820 --> 00:33:18,779
Mm, free trips
to the Bahamas...

668
00:33:18,866 --> 00:33:20,824
Think it's about dad?

669
00:33:20,911 --> 00:33:24,176
Well, thanks for chatting.

670
00:33:27,222 --> 00:33:28,919
What was that doctor saying?

671
00:33:29,007 --> 00:33:30,791
Well, he should probably
tell you himself.

672
00:33:30,878 --> 00:33:32,836
It's not really my place.

673
00:33:32,923 --> 00:33:36,623
Mr. Jane, people are suffering.
Tell us what you know.

674
00:33:36,710 --> 00:33:39,669
We're very sorry
for your loss.

675
00:33:39,756 --> 00:33:43,543
Oh, my God.
Oh, my God. He's gone.

676
00:33:43,630 --> 00:33:45,240
Son of a bitch.

677
00:33:45,327 --> 00:33:47,764
Can't help but feel
a little responsible here.

678
00:33:47,851 --> 00:33:49,375
- What'd you do to him?
- Serge.

679
00:33:49,462 --> 00:33:51,203
You were the last one
with him.

680
00:33:51,290 --> 00:33:53,466
If I find out
you did anything to him

681
00:33:53,553 --> 00:33:55,511
I swear you're gonna die.
You hear me?

682
00:33:55,598 --> 00:33:58,471
It's not a threat.
It's a promise.

683
00:33:58,558 --> 00:34:01,430
Shut... up.
Alright?

684
00:34:01,517 --> 00:34:03,171
You can't say that to me.

685
00:34:03,258 --> 00:34:05,173
You work for me.
I'm in charge now.

686
00:34:05,260 --> 00:34:07,088
No, you're not.

687
00:34:07,175 --> 00:34:09,047
I am.

688
00:34:09,134 --> 00:34:13,051
I talked to the crews,
all of them. They're with me.

689
00:34:13,138 --> 00:34:15,401
And we're gonna do this
smooth and smart

690
00:34:15,488 --> 00:34:17,577
and we're not gonna
go around threatening cops

691
00:34:17,664 --> 00:34:19,709
in public places.
Got it?

692
00:34:19,796 --> 00:34:21,276
- But you have--
- No.

693
00:34:21,363 --> 00:34:22,973
No, he's right. Wait.

694
00:34:23,061 --> 00:34:25,672
- We will talk at the house.
- You're in charge now?

695
00:34:25,759 --> 00:34:27,282
This is none of your business.

696
00:34:27,369 --> 00:34:30,894
You need to speak
with us alone.

697
00:34:30,981 --> 00:34:32,113
[chuckles]
Right.

698
00:34:32,200 --> 00:34:34,637
You really do.

699
00:34:36,161 --> 00:34:39,077
Wait here.

700
00:34:42,776 --> 00:34:45,431
So?

701
00:34:49,609 --> 00:34:51,567
- What the hell?
- It's an old trick.

702
00:34:51,654 --> 00:34:54,962
Small ball under the arm
stops the blood flowing.

703
00:34:55,049 --> 00:34:57,138
No pulse.

704
00:34:58,922 --> 00:35:01,751
He's alive. That's great.

705
00:35:01,838 --> 00:35:03,188
Not for you.

706
00:35:03,275 --> 00:35:05,407
You hired Raynor Marquette
to kill Junior

707
00:35:05,494 --> 00:35:07,888
because he was getting
in your way, didn't you?

708
00:35:07,975 --> 00:35:09,542
Good luck proving that.

709
00:35:09,629 --> 00:35:13,241
I don't have to prove it
in court. I'll just tell him.

710
00:35:20,857 --> 00:35:22,120
Don't do that.

711
00:35:22,207 --> 00:35:23,904
'I will if I have to.'

712
00:35:23,991 --> 00:35:26,428
'I think Marquette's
put one of my people in danger.'

713
00:35:26,515 --> 00:35:28,648
You're gonna
help us find him...

714
00:35:28,735 --> 00:35:32,130
or I will take you in there
and sign your death warrant.

715
00:35:32,217 --> 00:35:34,219
I think she means it.

716
00:35:35,872 --> 00:35:37,091
We got Marquette's cell phone.

717
00:35:37,178 --> 00:35:39,659
We were able to track it
to state route 4

718
00:35:39,746 --> 00:35:41,182
14 miles east
of Porchetto's cabin.

719
00:35:41,269 --> 00:35:42,488
He must be somewhere nearby.

720
00:35:42,575 --> 00:35:44,054
Yeah, it's pretty close
to here.

721
00:35:44,142 --> 00:35:47,319
I can get some rangers
to meet me there. Thanks.

722
00:35:47,406 --> 00:35:50,278
So do you ever think
about getting out of

723
00:35:50,365 --> 00:35:52,280
you know, sex work?

724
00:35:52,367 --> 00:35:54,369
What kind of car you got?

725
00:35:54,456 --> 00:35:56,719
Piece of crap, I bet.

726
00:35:56,806 --> 00:35:59,548
I drive a Lexus,
fully loaded.

727
00:35:59,635 --> 00:36:00,593
Oh, excuse me.

728
00:36:00,680 --> 00:36:01,768
[chuckles]

729
00:36:01,855 --> 00:36:03,291
There's more to life
than that.

730
00:36:03,378 --> 00:36:05,206
[crack]

731
00:36:05,293 --> 00:36:07,295
Get down.

732
00:36:07,382 --> 00:36:09,950
Stay here.
Don't make a sound.

733
00:36:16,348 --> 00:36:17,697
[gunshots]

734
00:36:23,703 --> 00:36:25,531
Grace Behind you.

735
00:36:25,618 --> 00:36:27,402
[grunting]

736
00:36:35,802 --> 00:36:37,195
Stop.

737
00:36:37,282 --> 00:36:40,589
- Get... off!
- Just... relax.

738
00:36:43,331 --> 00:36:46,247
So I guess we can
call it even now, huh?

739
00:36:48,118 --> 00:36:49,816
Bye, Grace

740
00:36:49,903 --> 00:36:52,514
Look after yourself.

741
00:36:54,255 --> 00:36:56,344
[Rigsby]
'Grace!
Where are you?!'

742
00:36:56,431 --> 00:37:01,436
Over here!

743
00:37:01,523 --> 00:37:02,742
You okay?

744
00:37:02,829 --> 00:37:05,875
Yeah, I'm fine.

745
00:37:07,442 --> 00:37:09,052
[door closes]

746
00:37:13,666 --> 00:37:16,146
This is your chance to do
something for yourself, Janpen.

747
00:37:16,234 --> 00:37:18,584
Marquette's still in the
hospital. You talk first

748
00:37:18,671 --> 00:37:22,022
the D.A. Will take first-degree
murder off the table.

749
00:37:25,068 --> 00:37:28,028
No death penalty.
You want that?

750
00:37:34,426 --> 00:37:37,603
Marquette and I are a team.

751
00:37:37,690 --> 00:37:41,215
Part of the job is
getting closer to the target.

752
00:37:41,302 --> 00:37:43,043
'That's what I do.'

753
00:37:52,226 --> 00:37:54,228
Nett had planted the gun.

754
00:37:54,315 --> 00:37:56,709
[Cho]
'Nett grabbed the gun
when he came out.'

755
00:37:56,796 --> 00:38:00,669
He took it to the fence.
Raynor was waiting.

756
00:38:00,756 --> 00:38:04,543
'We had to make it look like the
shooter came from the outside.'

757
00:38:04,630 --> 00:38:06,719
'That was nett's thing.'

758
00:38:06,806 --> 00:38:08,808
He was terrified
old man Porchetto

759
00:38:08,895 --> 00:38:11,463
would find out
he was behind it.

760
00:38:11,550 --> 00:38:15,815
When I was sleeping, you found
a cell signal, didn't you?

761
00:38:15,902 --> 00:38:18,383
That's how Marquette found us.
You called him.

762
00:38:18,470 --> 00:38:20,472
Just wanted to get out
of there.

763
00:38:20,559 --> 00:38:22,300
- By killing me.
- Oh.

764
00:38:22,387 --> 00:38:24,563
Well, it wasn't personal.

765
00:38:24,650 --> 00:38:26,042
Come on.

766
00:38:26,129 --> 00:38:28,958
I kind of like you. You know,
you're hardcore.

767
00:38:29,045 --> 00:38:32,266
I respect that.

768
00:38:32,353 --> 00:38:34,747
Let's go.

769
00:38:49,239 --> 00:38:50,197
Hey.

770
00:38:50,284 --> 00:38:53,113
Hey.

771
00:38:53,200 --> 00:38:55,898
How are you feeling?

772
00:38:55,985 --> 00:38:59,293
Better. Okay.

773
00:38:59,380 --> 00:39:00,686
Come here.

774
00:39:00,773 --> 00:39:02,862
[sighs]

775
00:39:03,732 --> 00:39:05,560
[Sarah]
'Hi.'

776
00:39:05,647 --> 00:39:09,347
Oh, hey.

777
00:39:09,434 --> 00:39:11,131
I heard you got back
alright.

778
00:39:11,218 --> 00:39:13,263
Yep. Safe and sound.

779
00:39:13,351 --> 00:39:16,571
Congratulations.
It's just such great news.

780
00:39:16,658 --> 00:39:17,920
I'll see you tomorrow,
Wayne.

781
00:39:18,007 --> 00:39:19,531
Yeah, see you tomorrow.

782
00:39:19,618 --> 00:39:20,619
Excuse me.

783
00:39:25,232 --> 00:39:26,973
You want to get
something to eat?

784
00:39:27,060 --> 00:39:30,759
Yeah. Absolutely.

785
00:39:34,241 --> 00:39:36,678
I'm sorry
if that was uncomfortable.

786
00:39:36,765 --> 00:39:41,117
It didn't mean anything.
Really. Nothing at all.

787
00:39:41,204 --> 00:39:44,251
No, it's okay.
Wayne, I understand.

788
00:39:48,255 --> 00:39:50,518
So... how have you been?

789
00:39:50,605 --> 00:39:53,347
Good. Fine.

790
00:39:53,434 --> 00:39:56,655
I'm pregnant.

791
00:40:14,890 --> 00:40:15,848
Jane?

792
00:40:15,935 --> 00:40:17,719
Mm-hmm.

793
00:40:17,806 --> 00:40:20,679
I'm sorry to ask this,
but..

794
00:40:20,766 --> 00:40:24,465
do you ever talk
to your wife?

795
00:40:24,552 --> 00:40:26,859
Yes, sometimes.

796
00:40:26,946 --> 00:40:28,469
Do you ever see her?

797
00:40:28,556 --> 00:40:30,428
No, never.

798
00:40:30,515 --> 00:40:33,082
If you did see her..

799
00:40:33,169 --> 00:40:34,736
...would you think
you were crazy?

800
00:40:34,823 --> 00:40:38,348
Ah.

801
00:40:38,436 --> 00:40:40,612
Craig came to see you,
didn't he?

802
00:40:40,699 --> 00:40:41,787
Yeah.

803
00:40:41,874 --> 00:40:44,746
What did he want?

804
00:40:44,833 --> 00:40:47,575
I don't know.

805
00:40:47,662 --> 00:40:50,535
This will sound
really weird, but..

806
00:40:50,622 --> 00:40:52,450
...he kind of saved my life.

807
00:40:52,537 --> 00:40:54,364
Figuratively speaking,
I hope.

808
00:40:54,452 --> 00:40:58,499
Yes. I mean, he wasn't...
really there, but..

809
00:40:58,586 --> 00:41:00,762
You can't decide what to do
with the necklace

810
00:41:00,849 --> 00:41:05,245
because it reminds you
of your past.

811
00:41:05,332 --> 00:41:07,639
You can try to forget it..

812
00:41:07,726 --> 00:41:09,989
...or you can learn
to live with it.

813
00:41:10,076 --> 00:41:11,425
Yeah.

814
00:41:11,512 --> 00:41:13,558
Hmm.

815
00:41:15,081 --> 00:41:17,257
Well?

816
00:41:17,344 --> 00:41:19,520
Well what?

817
00:41:19,607 --> 00:41:23,916
What do you think I should do?
Keep it or get rid of it?

818
00:41:29,356 --> 00:41:33,186
Well, I think
that's your call, Grace.

819
00:41:33,273 --> 00:41:35,623
Don't you?

820
00:41:36,972 --> 00:41:38,800
Goodnight.

821
00:41:38,887 --> 00:41:41,977
Goodnight, Jane.

822
00:41:44,937 --> 00:41:47,374
[clink]

